```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: LLM training-data engineers running web-scale near-dedup (C4/RedPajama/The Stack) with MinHash-LSH → connected-components → keep-one; they need to avoid transitively deleting diverse docs that are not near-duplicates of any retained doc.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Structural mechanism is real (not LSH artifact) but magnitude in production is unproven — 0.724 ±0.003 innocent-removal at T=0.8 is from synthetic drift-chains; packet explicitly flags that “magnitude hinges on whether real near-dup graphs at T~0.8 contain DRIFT-CHAINS or are predominantly tight CLIQUES” and “harness PROVES the graph-theoretic core but CANNOT settle real-corpus chain PREVALENCE.” MinHash (production) cuts the effect to 0.323 (vs 0.724 exact), and at T=0.9 the effect collapses to ~0. Without L1 measurement of chain prevalence in a real corpus slice and downstream diversity/eval-loss impact, the win is a plausible microbenchmark, not an operationally confirmed production gain.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [1] Pipeline inertia — CC keep-one is the de-facto standard (Lee2021 2107.06499; BigCode dedup blog) and is presented as desirable (Lee’s 200K-doc C4 component is chaining); [2] Mitigation cost — SemDeDup-style non-transitive (2303.09540) requires changing the deletion predicate; complete-linkage is O(n²) per component and impractical at scale; [3] Evidence gap — teams need L1 proof that real T=0.8 graphs contain enough drift-chains (revision histories, template-drift, paraphrase ladders) to justify the switch, and that the “innocent” docs are not redundant (downstream harm unmeasured); [4] Threshold sensitivity — if operators move to T=0.9, chains break and the benefit vanishes.]
RATIONALE: Packet L0 shows CC innocent-removal = 0.724 ±0.003 at realistic T=0.8 (moderate density, EXACT) vs 0.000 for SemDeDup non-transitive and complete-linkage; effect persists with exact edges (0.724) and is larger than with MinHash (0.323), proving it is a transitive-closure topology issue, not an LSH-FP artifact. However, the same packet records the honest boundary: “effect COLLAPSES to ~0 at T=0.9 because drift-chains break” and “whether such chains are prevalent in real corpora at T~0.8 is the load-bearing empirical question for L1.” No real-corpus chain-prevalence or downstream model-quality data is provided. Therefore the claim is a valid structural finding with an actionable negative result (if graphs are cliquey, CC is fine), but the operational win for production dedup remains insufficiently evidenced.
```
